---
import LegalPage from "../../components/LegalPage.astro";
import {
  deletionWarnings,
  keepAfterStopPaying,
  minimumAge,
  operator,
  paymentProvider,
  retentionRows,
} from "../../content/legal";
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy"
  description="What DMbot keeps about you, who sees it, how long we keep it, and how to delete it."
  heading="Privacy"
  summary="DMbot only records people who said yes. We never keep the sound of your voice: it is turned into text and the sound is thrown away. Everyone in your Discord server can read what was written down. We keep your Discord account number, your email and which of your servers use DMbot, so you can sign in and use your plan. We don't sell anything about you, and there are no ads. You can stop being recorded at any time, and you can delete your account and your campaigns from My account."
>
  <h2>Who looks after your information</h2>
  <p>
    DMbot is run by {operator.name}, {operator.address}. Write to {operator.email} about anything
    on this page.
  </p>

  <h2>What we keep</h2>
  <h3>When you sign in to this website</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Your <strong>Discord user id</strong> and the <strong>email</strong> Discord gives us. We
      use the email only to tell you about your account and plan.
    </li>
    <li>
      The <strong>ids of your Discord servers that use DMbot</strong>, so we can show them to
      you. {"{{CHECK: confirm with #435 what /me stores}}"}
    </li>
    <li>
      Sign-in uses Discord. We never see your Discord password, and we don't keep your Discord
      sign-in token after you sign out. {"{{CHECK: confirm once sign-in is built (#435)}}"}
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>When DMbot is in your game</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Your yes.</strong> When you press "I consent", we keep the date, the wording you
      agreed to, and how you agreed. That's how we prove you said yes.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>What was said.</strong> The words of people who said yes, written down as text, with
      the time they were said. Nobody else is ever recorded, and bots are never recorded.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your campaign.</strong> The names, places and notes your table makes, the game
      master's notes and settings, and any adventure or rulebook text the game master shares.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your voice is not kept.</strong> The sound is sent to be written down, then thrown
      away. It is never saved.
      {"{{CHECK: when the re-listen feature ships, say it holds about a minute of sound in memory only}}"}
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>When you pay</h3>
  <p>
    Payments go through {paymentProvider}. They are the seller, and they hold your card or
    PayPal details; we never see them. They tell us your plan, whether it's paid, and when it
    renews.
  </p>

  <h2>Who can see it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>What was said</strong> can be read and downloaded by everyone in the Discord server
      where the game is played (downloads come with paid plans). The question you say yes to
      tells you this.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The game master's (DM's) notes</strong>: each campaign picks who sees them. Only the
      game master; players who choose to peek (the usual setting, with a spoiler warning first);
      or everyone in the server. When a player peeks, the game master can see who peeked.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Backups</strong> of a paid campaign hold the campaign, including the game master's
      secrets, and anyone in the server may download one.
      {"{{CHECK: say whether transcripts are in backups once that is built}}"} This keeps a campaign safe if
      its game master leaves.
    </li>
    <li>Only people in your server can open your campaign in DMbot. Campaigns never share information.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Companies that help us</h2>
  <p>We share only what each one needs to do its job:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Discord</strong>: where DMbot runs, and how you sign in.</li>
    <li><strong>Deepgram</strong>: turns the sound of people who said yes into text.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Anthropic</strong>: the AI that helps with names, rules and story notes. It gets the
      text it needs, not sound.
    </li>
    <li><strong>{paymentProvider}</strong>: takes payments.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare</strong>: delivers this website. {"{{CHECK: once the owner sets it up}}"}
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>{"{{HOSTING PROVIDER}}"}</strong>: the server DMbot and its database run on.
      {"{{CHECK: name and country}}"}
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Some of these companies are in the United States. {"{{CHECK: transfer safeguards for people in the EU and UK}}"}
  </p>
  <p>We don't sell your information and we don't use it for ads.</p>
  <p>
    If a server uses its own AI or speech key, we keep that key locked (encrypted), use it only
    for that server, and never show it in full.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>A campaign is deleted this long after its last game:</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
  <table>
    <caption>How long a campaign is kept after its last game, by plan</caption>
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Plan</th><th scope="col">Kept after the last game</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {
        retentionRows.map((row) => (
          <tr>
            <td>{row.plan}</td>
            <td>{row.keep}</td>
          </tr>
        ))
      }
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    If a plan stops being paid, its campaigns are kept for {keepAfterStopPaying}. We message the
    game master on Discord {deletionWarnings} before anything is deleted.
    Backups people already downloaded are theirs to keep or delete.
  </p>
  <p>Account details are deleted when you delete your account. {"{{CHECK: anything payment law says we must keep, such as invoices}}"}</p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Stop being recorded</strong> at any time: press "Stop recording me" in the message
      DMbot sends you, or type <code>/consent revoke</code> in Discord.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Delete your account</strong> from <a href="/account">My account</a>. This removes
      your sign-in details, your plan and the campaigns you own, straight away. Lines you said in
      someone else's campaign stay there, readable by that server, until that campaign is
      deleted. {"{{CHECK: what account deletion removes (#435), and update when \"Delete my past transcripts\" ships}}"}
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Ask for a copy</strong> of what we keep, or ask us to fix it, by writing to
      {operator.email}. {"{{CHECK: rights under GDPR, UK GDPR and US state laws, and how fast we must answer}}"}
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This website uses one cookie, only to keep you signed in. Other websites can't read it. There
    are no tracking or ad cookies. {"{{CHECK: confirm with #435}}"}
  </p>

  <h2>Keeping it safe</h2>
  <p>
    Everything travels over a locked (encrypted) connection. Keys and secrets are stored
    encrypted, and our logs hold ids, never what you said or your payment details.
    {"{{CHECK: say how the database itself is encrypted on the server}}"}
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    You must be at least {minimumAge} to use Discord, so you must be at least {minimumAge} to use
    DMbot. {"{{CHECK: older age where local law requires it, for example 16 in some EU countries}}"}
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we change what we keep or who sees it, we'll update this page and tell signed-in users. If
    the question you said yes to changes, DMbot asks you again before it records you.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
